  "source_route_assessment": {
    "result": "The actual map sheet provides a source-specific match to the treaty-described 1336–1337 segment: the sheet names Tigiretskiy/Stamoviy Belok ridges, labels heights 1975.9 and 2170.3, and shows geodetic point 2189.7 at the southeast turn. The Russian Annex description says the line runs generally south along the ridges through those heights for 11.3 km to point 1337. This materially supports applicability of the retained source for investigating these contacts.",
    "adverse_context": "The native sheet has dense red linework and contours over the ridge; the legend distinguishes the red state-boundary symbol, but red relief/contour ink overlaps visually. At the two transformed center positions, the rendered corridor does not expose a unique, sharp side-defining boundary stroke. The map-to-ground transformation is conditional on Pulkovo 1942 / Gauss-Kruger zone 14; an undatum alternative was also retained. Neither transformation or manual pixel precision is map positional accuracy.",
    "other_text": "The immediately prior segment has an unresolved 901.7 versus 1901.7 discrepancy between Russian Adilet text and UN English. It is not used to identify the 1336–1337 segment, whose listed heights agree."
  },
  "placement_review": {
    "method": "Independently inspected retained native raster and a fresh 200x200 crop from its native pixels. Reviewed the recorded local two-dimensional affine fit, four fitted grid crossings and two distinct held-out crossings. The fit residuals are about 0.25 px per component; held-out discrepancies are 0.5 px. Those values characterize this local registration only.",
    "position": "The assessment’s conditional and no-datum placements for both keys land in or immediately beside the same broad ridge/boundary ink corridor. At the crop scale, dense contours and overlapping red map marks prevent assignment to a unique side. This is not evidence that either point lies on a specific sovereign side.",
    "artifact_note": "Two crop paths listed in the earlier assessment (/tmp/m4448-two-key-plain.png and /tmp/m4448-registered-two-key-detail.png) were absent when checked. I independently cropped the already-retained native JPEG to /tmp/m44-48-independent-detail.jpg and inspected it. No download or rerender of the source PDF was done. The coordinator separately reports that copies of those crop files existed in the coordinator environment; I did not access or verify those copies or their hashes. The paths were absent in my filesystem check, and my finding relies on the independently viewed native JPEG crop recorded below.",
    "absent_crop_paths": [
      "/tmp/m4448-two-key-plain.png",
      "/tmp/m4448-registered-two-key-detail.png"
    ]
  },
  "independent_conclusion": {
    "disposition": "A narrowly scoped, researched-unresolved proposal for these two exact keys is supported; keep their native holds. The primary route evidence materially identifies the correct map segment, but the source image plus conditional local placement does not resolve which side contains either key. This is a source-specific ambiguity after meaningful map and treaty examination, not a blanket rule requiring modern authority or certified datum evidence.",
    "positive_path": "No positive per-key assignment is justified from the available image because neither point has a uniquely resolved relation to the boundary stroke. A new producer is not warranted solely to restate this finding.",
    "limits": [
      "No sovereignty/current-law conclusion from labels or geometry.",
      "No map accuracy inferred from grid-fit residuals or coordinate-operation accuracy.",
      "No full package disposition or change to any native hold."
    ]
  },
