  "effort_and_actual_evidence": [
    "Joined the exact original tuple and source-contact roster: Belyayevsky District, KAZ Aktobe Region ordinal 8, coordinate [56.72795099288237,51.018820157290016], selected treaty sheet M-40-30, album70, bundle 09 sheets68–88.",
    "Opened and examined the full official Russian 2005 treaty and Annex 1 from the linked legacy Adilet record. Article 3 identifies the Annex 2 map as boundary evidence; Article 4 distinguishes natural channel changes from the treaty line. Annex text includes points306–308 (Urta-Burtya/Burtya/Tarangul) and339–341 (Kiyaly-Burtya/Kiya/Baysai). These passages are not geographically joined to this key; the earlier Ilek 244–247 passage is expressly not used because it is distant from M40-30.",
    "The official UN treaty map-bundle response for bundle09 is retained and contains a contents page, not the M-40-30 sheet. This exact sheet is missing from the acquired response.",
    "The published official Adilet PDF, DOCX, and law.gov publication endpoints each returned HTTP404 with retained bodies. These are endpoint-not-found outcomes, not access denials; the failed identical requests were not repeated.",
    "Focused additional searches for M-40-30 and the exact Annex/map returned no authenticated sheet. Search surfaced legalacts.egov.kz/npa/view?id=14762268; opening its search result showed an archived 2023 integrity-check bill consultation, unrelated to the treaty/map.",
    "Opened official National Geological Service home and map-materials page. The latter lists thematic products and a 1996 Mineral Resources atlas at1:4m/1:2m, not the local topo/treaty sheet. Opened the agency notice that its former geological-report catalogue was discontinued and followed its successor EPN link; the public registry showed report-search fields and70,844 records, with no local map identified.",
    "The National Geological Service homepage links an interactive GIS at https://gis.geology.gov.kz/geo/. Its first web-reader open returned HTTP502; one bounded repeat of that same URL returned “not accessible via this tool” without an HTTP status/body. Neither is an access-denial determination.",
    "Searched Rosreestr’s State Catalogue/open-data source for exact local river-name variants; the catalogue page timed out, and the exact-name site queries yielded no indexed records. No map or location record was obtained."
  ],
  "scientific_conclusion": {
    "positive_assignment": "Not supported: no source-specific geographical relationship between this exact key and a treaty-described boundary segment has been established. Contact/region names and coordinates alone do not prove side or boundary position.",
    "researched_unresolved": "The bounded evidence supports a genuinely researched-unresolved proposal for this exact key, with its native hold unchanged. The proposal is supported by completed, source-specific investigation and repeated official-record attempts that did not return the relevant sheet; it does not rely merely on the map being missing. The unresolved factual issue is precise: where [56.72795099288237,51.018820157290016] lies relative to the treaty’s mapped boundary and locally described channel/feature, which Annex 1 prose alone does not locate.",
    "scope": "This is not positive repair, sovereign attribution, legal clearance, whole-package completion, or root acceptance.",
    "remaining_step": "No additional concrete, relevant, publicly readable primary item was identified in the opened official sources. If a direct M-40-30 map body or other point-localizing treaty record becomes available, compare it to this exact key before any positive assignment. That is a bounded future opportunity, not a universal certificate or an exhaustive-search condition."
  },
